From: Medvedolog <noreply@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: cubie-a5e: keep Wi-Fi BLDO1 enabled

The AXP717 BLDO1 rail supplies 1.8 V SDIO I/O to the AIC8800D80.
Keep it enabled regardless of regulator consumer transitions. The
existing mmc1 vqmmc-supply reference remains unchanged.

Ported from Armbian:
patch/kernel/archive/sunxi-6.18/patches.backports/
34-fix-wifi-regulator-cubie-a5e.patch
Original author: Juan Sanchez Fuentes <juanesf91@gmail.com>

This is a hardware experiment; it does not establish that the SDIO
firmware -110 timeouts are due to regulator shutdown.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-a527-cubie-a5e.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-a527-cubie-a5e.dts
@@ -263,6 +263,7 @@ reg_aldo4: aldo4 {
			};

			reg_bldo1: bldo1 {
+				regulator-always-on;
				regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
				regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
				regulator-name = "vcc-pg-iowifi";
-- 
2.47.0
